  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Bezalel can be divided into the preposition ב, צל ‘shadow’, and אל ‘God’. The lists in Ezra 2:52 and Neh 7:54 supply the name Bazluth or Bazlith but give no explanation linking it to onions or peeling. Neither personal name is assigned to this plant. The Geʿez and Tigre words are recorded as probable Arabic loans."
